Third-party material referenced but NOT included
--------------------------------------------------

The following are used by this project but are not redistributed in this
repository, because this project does not hold the right to redistribute
them. You will need to obtain each of these yourself if you want to rebuild
or flash anything here; see `docs/toolchain.md` and
`docs/clean-room-rebuild.md` for exactly how each is used.

- **Bose's own firmware** for this product (any `.dfu`, extracted
  filesystem content, voice prompts, or disassembly listing of it). This
  project's tools operate on a copy you download directly from Bose.
- **The CSR/Qualcomm ADK** (versions 4.3.1 and 4.4) and its bundled
  BlueSuite tools — vendor-licensed development kits for CSR867x-family
  Bluetooth chips, obtained separately from Qualcomm/CSR's own
  distribution for chip developers.
- **CSR's "AN093" DFU File Format Specification** — a vendor document
  whose own text carries a non-disclosure notice; this project's own
  independent, clean-room re-derivation of the parts of that format it
  needs is in `docs/dfu-signature-scheme.md` and `tools/csr/`, not a copy
  of or excerpt from that document.
- **`bose-dfu`**, the third-party command-line tool this project's flash
  scripts invoke to talk to the speaker's USB DFU interface (not bundled;
  obtain it from its own upstream project, `tchebb/bose-dfu`
  (https://github.com/tchebb/bose-dfu), and credit it there).
- **`innoextract`**, used only to unpack the ADK's Inno Setup installers;
  a separate, independently licensed (zlib/Boost-family) tool, not bundled.

Derived reference tables
--------------------------

`tools/csr/pskeys_gordon.json`, `tools/traps-bluelab73.json`, and
`tools/traps-bluelab74.json` are name-to-number lookup tables (persistent-store
key names, firmware trap names), derived by this project from the ADK's own
header files during development. They are facts about an interface (names and
numbers), not creative content, and are also documented independently elsewhere
by others working with this chip family.

`build/hook/slack_pool.json` holds derived linear-algebra coefficients (a digest
function's measured per-position contribution, computed by probing the vendor
build tool as a black-box oracle — see `docs/dfu-signature-scheme.md`), not a
copy of any stock firmware bytes. Separately, `docs/FACTS.md` (fact F263) quotes
one 10-word official persistent-store default value, identical across every
released firmware version for this product (not device-specific, not secret —
config defaults, not content), for documentation completeness.

